# Scheduled workflows that do NOT (yet) report their red through the ci-failure ledger pair or a
# standing sentinel issue (check-scheduled-lane-reporters.py, MeshWeaver#7416).
#
# A scheduled run reaches no pull request, no reviewer and no check list, so its red is red in an
# empty room unless something durable carries it. lock-pinned-digests.yml was red for six days that
# way. The template is that file's `cause` / `lane-red` / `lane-green` jobs.
#
# Each line: <workflow file>  — <why it may stand without one>. The list only SHRINKS: an entry for a
# workflow that is gone, has no schedule, or now reports is stale and reds the gate. A NEW scheduled
# workflow gets a reporter, never a line here.

# Report through a mechanism of their own, which this gate does not recognise by shape.
control-always-latest.yml  — files, comments on and closes its own `control-lag` issue in the alarm step itself (policy control-always-latest); a red of an EARLIER step is not filed — debt
main-cd.yml  — its scheduled tick is the delivery reconciler, and a failed delivery is filed on main-cd's own `ci-failure` issue with a heal ledger

# The schedule is a catch-up sweep of a pull-request lane; its subject is open pull requests, whose
# own checks show the outcome.
request-review-on-change.yml  — the 15-minute tick re-judges open pull requests for a missed review request; the per-PR effect is visible on each PR
review-answered.yml  — the 15-minute tick re-judges PENDING review verdicts (policy review-pending-while-answering); a missed tick leaves a verdict pending (still blocking, never green) on its PR, which names it
stage-advance.yml  — the tick re-releases held PR heads whose review event was missed; a held head is visible on its PR as a pending stage

# There is no KNOWN DEBT section any more: the last four lanes that reported nowhere
# (arm-credential, dockerhub-mirror, prod-synthetic-probe, shared-rules) carry the ledger pair.
